51
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:51,820
So cold.

52
00:03:51,820 --> 00:03:56,200
Hang on.

53
00:03:56,560 --> 00:03:58,340
Father will be back soon, all right?

54
00:03:58,340 --> 00:03:59,340
No.

55
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:29,320
That day...

56
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:32,140
I lost two people who were dear to me.

57
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:36,440
Both my mother and my father passed away.

58
00:04:38,860 --> 00:04:42,060
I was ten years old, without any parents.

59
00:04:43,220 --> 00:04:45,900
I was ten years old and completely alone.

60
00:04:49,220 --> 00:04:53,320
No, that's not right.

61
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:56,300
I was eleven when I found myself alone.

62
00:04:56,300 --> 00:05:01,420
Before then, I used to have a twin brother.

63
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:06,120
An older brother, and his name was Yuichiro.

64
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:12,980
Kindness does no good for anyone.

65
00:05:13,500 --> 00:05:16,760
If you try to help somebody in need, you'll only get hurt.

66
00:05:17,940 --> 00:05:19,020
That's not true.

67
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:24,680
Whatever you do to help others has a way of coming back around and helping yourself someday.

68
00:05:25,260 --> 00:05:26,600
That's what father said.

69
00:05:26,600 --> 00:05:31,960
You're regurgitating the words of a man who got himself killed trying to help someone else.

70
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:35,300
How could you say something so cold?

71
00:05:35,660 --> 00:05:37,520
He died trying to save our mother.

72
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:41,200
As if a few herbs would have done anything to heal her at that point.

73
00:05:41,820 --> 00:05:42,920
Don't be so stupid.

74
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:45,500
Don't say such awful things.

75
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:50,760
If he hadn't gone out in the middle of a storm, maybe we would have only lost our mother that night.

76
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:53,200
Please stop saying things like that.

77
00:05:53,380 --> 00:05:54,560
That's going too far.

78
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:56,760
I'm only telling you how it is.

79
00:05:57,160 --> 00:05:58,780
And stop being so noisy.

80
00:05:59,220 --> 00:06:00,420
You might attract boars.

81
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:04,920
I guess the Mu and Muichiro stands for incompetence.

82
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:07,160
This conversation is meaningless.

83
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:09,920
After all, you can't change the past.

84
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:13,840
Or maybe the Mu and Muichiro stands for meaningless.

85
00:06:13,840 --> 00:06:24,520
He was unsympathetic and spoke harshly.

86
00:06:25,280 --> 00:06:30,180
I feel that, in a way, I acted like him after I had amnesia.

87
00:06:33,060 --> 00:06:34,920
Life with my brother wasn't easy.

88
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:37,240
If anything, it was stifling.

89
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:40,260
I was sure he despised me.

90
00:06:40,260 --> 00:06:44,720
And because of that, I couldn't help but think of him as a cold person.

91
00:06:46,300 --> 00:06:48,660
I remember the seasons changed.

92
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:51,020
And it was spring.

93
00:06:53,900 --> 00:06:55,080
I'll be back.

94
00:06:55,540 --> 00:06:56,820
I'm gonna fetch some water.

95
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:59,160
You still haven't gotten any?

96
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:01,160
Hmm.

97
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:25,820
The first time I saw her, I couldn't believe it.

98
00:07:25,820 --> 00:07:27,900
She was so beautiful.

99
00:07:28,540 --> 00:07:30,840
I thought she was a white birch spirit.

100
00:07:30,840 --> 00:07:46,160
It turns out, this person was the Master's wife, who came to visit us.

101
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:49,200
Which meant she traveled all the way up the mountain.

102
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:59,800
But, in the end, my brother just spewed his usual insults and drove Lady Amane away.

103
00:08:01,580 --> 00:08:02,800
Can you believe it?

104
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:05,120
She says our ancestors were swordsmen.

105
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:10,620
Apparently, we're descendants of an amazing swordsman who used something called first breathing.

106
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:11,940
Why should I care?

107
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:13,480
Wash the rice already.

108
00:08:13,480 --> 00:08:16,000
Hey, let's become swordsmen.

109
00:08:16,340 --> 00:08:19,440
It's hard to believe demons exist and are out there hurting people.

110
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:21,840
If we can do something to help, we should.

111
00:08:22,160 --> 00:08:22,520
Right?

112
00:08:22,940 --> 00:08:26,080
So let's become swordsmen and save the people who are suffering.

113
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:27,480
If we do it together...

114
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:44,540
What makes you think you could ever save anybody?

115
00:08:44,980 --> 00:08:49,060
You can't cook rice on your own and you're gonna be a swordsman and save others?

116
00:08:49,500 --> 00:08:51,300
Give me a break, Muiichiro!

117
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:55,180
You sound like mother and father spouting that kind of nonsense.

118
00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:57,120
Stop being so optimistic.

119
00:08:57,480 --> 00:08:58,620
Your mind is poisoned.

120
00:08:59,120 --> 00:09:03,060
Just like mother who told us she was fine and then worked until she collapsed.

121
00:09:03,300 --> 00:09:06,020
Like father who got killed trying to find some herbs.

122
00:09:06,540 --> 00:09:09,540
Even after I tried to stop him.

123
00:09:10,060 --> 00:09:13,580
Even after I begged mother to rest over and over.

124
00:09:14,100 --> 00:09:18,880
The only kind of people who can help others are people who were chosen to do so.

125
00:09:19,380 --> 00:09:23,460
Our ancestors may have been swordsmen, but we are just two hopeless orphans.

126
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:25,880
People like us are useless.

127
00:09:25,880 --> 00:09:27,980
We're only good for one thing.

128
00:09:28,460 --> 00:09:30,400
And that's dying in the street like dogs.

129
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:33,160
Our parents met the same fate to prove it.

130
00:09:33,660 --> 00:09:35,940
We'll only end up getting used by that woman.

131
00:09:36,300 --> 00:09:38,040
Why do you think she came all the way here?

132
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:40,640
We're never talking about this again, got it?

133
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:42,680
Now hurry up and get dinner ready!

134
00:09:46,780 --> 00:09:52,780
After that incident, we stopped speaking to each other.

135
00:09:55,780 --> 00:10:02,960
Except for the one time we fought briefly when my brother hurled water at Lady Amane, who traveled up the mountain to visit us again.

136
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:32,940
We're never talking to each other.

137
